Z||000010||fieroX||10-31-2001||06:20 PM||||with nitrous you acclerate off the line, then hit the switch, (you dont want to hit it right off the line because you will only boil your tires, plus you have to maintain a certain rpm before you hit it, 3000+)  when you hit the switch its like accelerating all over again, but from a roll.  Its awesome.  Ive driven my friends car to a 13.02 at 105 with nitrous.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fierox.com/logo2small.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000011||NOS3800||10-31-2001||06:35 PM||||The way my NOS is hooked up is different then most. It feeds off the TPS sensor on the 3800. At wide open throttle the TPS puts out a 4.3V current. My ZEX kit reads this then opens the NOS solenoid and then you have to HANG the F*** on! I grip the steering wheel real tight! I swear the car feels like it is leaving me behind! Its an all or nothing deal, unless you have a progressive set up. BTW, mine activates at any rpm, as long as its at WOT. Most kits use a micro switch on the Throttle arm on the throttle body to tell the solenoid to open. Like a hammer hitting a button. You don't push a button to spray the NOS, thats usualy done by the two methods described. But you have to flick a switch to turn everything on, an "arming" switch. I have an aircraft style switch that has a safety cover, flip the cover up, then the switch, push the gas and GOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOoooooooooooo.........!<P>------------------<BR>Purple 1988 GT<BR>NOS injected 3800 Series II V6<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sig_Pic,_nos3800_3.jpg"> <BR>Best ET(75 shot)-13.21@102.13 mph<BR>w/o NOS 14.86@92.06mph||||reg||10
Z||000012||NOS3800||10-31-2001||06:37 PM||||BTW, I try to soil my pants but my butt cheeks are clinched too tight!!!||||reg||10
